INT. ABANDONED PLANETARIUM - NIGHT

Dust. A cracked dome. The projector sits in the center like a sleeping insect. Three flashlights wander across the ceiling, snagging on fallen plaster.

GRETA "GIGI" HALVORSEN (17, hoodie, camera around her neck) climbs onto the star-seat rail. DESMOND "DEZ" OYELARAN-PRICE (18, varsity jacket, sweating) follows. MARISOL "MARI" CASTELLANOS (17, headlamp, cracked phone) stays at the door, one hand on the frame.

GIGI
Dez. Mari. Check it out. It's still plugged in.

DEZ
Gigi, nothing here is plugged in.

GIGI
Tell that to the little red light.

She points. A tiny red diode on the projector's base, glowing steadily. Dez swallows. Mari lowers her phone.

MARI
Gigi, I'm serious. Let's go.

GIGI
We came all this way, Mari.

MARI
We came because you dared us. I'm daring us the other way.

DEZ
She has a point, Gigi.

GIGI
You two are such babies.

She crosses to the projector and wipes the dust from the lens with her sleeve. Dez hovers at her shoulder, and Mari edges in from the doorway, until all three huddle around the old machine, flashlights pooled on its brass.

DEZ
Don't touch the switch.

GIGI
Don't tell me what to touch.

MARI
Seriously, Gigi, don't.

Gigi touches the switch. Click. Nothing. Then, far overhead, a hum. The dome fills with stars: soft, warm, and wrong, slowly drifting out of order, constellations sliding into new shapes.

MARI (CONT'D)
That's not the sky.

DEZ
It's a planetarium, Mari. It's supposed to not be the sky.

GIGI
(whispering)
It's beautiful.

She raises her camera and the shutter clicks. Stars turn. The shapes settle into letters, then words. All three read them together without meaning to.

DEZ
"Gigi. Dez. Mari."

MARI
It knows our names.

GIGI
(lowering the camera)
It's a trick. Someone planned this.

DEZ
Who? Nobody knew we were coming.

MARI
I told no one. I swear.

GIGI
Then who wrote it?

The stars shift again. One more word, slowly forming.

"STAY."
